{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_div = 1\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            largest_div = max(largest_div, i)\n            # n // i is the other divisor. It will be larger than i unless i == sqrt(n)\n            # It will always be smaller than n for i > 1.\n            largest_div = max(largest_div, n // i)\n    return largest_div"}
