{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "def monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_increasing = True\n    is_decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(len(l) - 1):\n        if l[i] > l[i+1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n        if l[i] < l[i+1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n        \n        # If the list is neither strictly increasing nor strictly decreasing,\n        # it cannot be monotonic. We can stop early.\n        if not is_increasing and not is_decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "def monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    increasing = decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] > l[i - 1]:\n            decreasing = False\n        elif l[i] < l[i - 1]:\n            increasing = False\n\n        if not increasing and not decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
