{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    sign = '-' if x < 0 else ''\n    digits = str(abs(x))\n    n = len(digits)\n\n    if shift <= n:\n        # Perform right circular shift\n        shifted_digits = digits[-shift:] + digits[:-shift]\n    else:\n        # Reverse digits\n        shifted_digits = digits[::-1]\n\n    return sign + shifted_digits"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_x = str(x)\n    n = len(s_x)\n\n    if shift > n:\n        return s_x[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Calculate effective shift for values up to n, where shift=n means no change\n        effective_shift = shift % n\n        if effective_shift == 0:\n            return s_x\n        \n        # Perform right circular shift\n        return s_x[n - effective_shift:] + s_x[:n - effective_shift]"}
