{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of a triangle given its side lengths, rounded to 2 decimal points.\n    Returns -1 if the sides do not form a valid triangle.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if sides are positive and satisfy the triangle inequality theorem\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0 and\n            a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n\n    # Calculate the area using Heron's formula\n    area = math.sqrt(s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c))\n\n    return round(area, 2)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return the area of\n    the triangle rounded to 2 decimal points if the three sides form a valid triangle. \n    Otherwise return -1\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if sides are positive\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0 or c <= 0:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Check triangle inequality\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n\n    # Calculate area using Heron's formula\n    area_squared = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n    \n    # Ensure area_squared is not negative due to floating point inaccuracies\n    if area_squared < 0:\n        area_squared = 0 # This effectively means area is 0, for degenerate triangles\n\n    area = math.sqrt(area_squared)\n\n    # Round the area to 2 decimal points\n    return round(area, 2)"}
