{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "def closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Returns the closest integer to the given string representation of a number.\n    Equidistant numbers are rounded away from zero.\n    '''\n    f_val = float(value)\n    integer_part = int(f_val)\n    fractional_part = f_val - integer_part\n\n    if f_val >= 0:\n        if fractional_part >= 0.5:\n            return integer_part + 1\n        else:\n            return integer_part\n    else: # f_val < 0\n        if fractional_part <= -0.5:\n            return integer_part - 1\n        else:\n            return integer_part"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "def closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Create a function that takes a value (string) representing a number\n    and returns the closest integer to it. If the number is equidistant\n    from two integers, round it away from zero.\n    '''\n    f_value = float(value)\n\n    # Calculate the integer part by truncating towards zero\n    integer_part_towards_zero = int(f_value)\n    # Calculate the fractional part\n    fractional_part = f_value - integer_part_towards_zero\n\n    # Custom tie-breaking rule: round away from zero for .5 cases\n    if fractional_part == 0.5:\n        return integer_part_towards_zero + 1\n    elif fractional_part == -0.5:\n        return integer_part_towards_zero - 1\n    else:\n        # For other cases, use Python's built-in round function\n        # which rounds to the nearest even number for .5 ties,\n        # but for non-.5 values, it rounds to the nearest integer as required.\n        return int(round(f_value))"}
