{"task_id": "HumanEval/136", "solution": "from typing import List, Optional, Tuple\n\ndef largest_smallest_integers(lst: List[int]) -> Tuple[Optional[int], Optional[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a tuple (largest_negative, smallest_positive) from the input list.\n    Zero values are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_negative: Optional[int] = None\n    smallest_positive: Optional[int] = None\n\n    for num in lst:\n        if num < 0:\n            if largest_negative is None or num > largest_negative:\n                largest_negative = num\n        elif num > 0:\n            if smallest_positive is None or num < smallest_positive:\n                smallest_positive = num\n\n    return largest_negative, smallest_positive"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/137", "solution": "def compare_one(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two inputs (int, float, or string representing a number) and returns\n    the larger value preserving its original type, or None if equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _parse_value(value):\n        \"\"\"Converts an input to its numeric float representation.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            return float(value)\n        elif isinstance(value, str):\n            return float(value.replace(',', '.'))\n        return value # Should not happen based on problem description but included for completeness\n\n    numeric_a = _parse_value(a)\n    numeric_b = _parse_value(b)\n\n    if numeric_a > numeric_b:\n        return a\n    elif numeric_b > numeric_a:\n        return b\n    else:\n        return None"}
