{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns even integers between a and b, inclusive, in ascending order.\n    Handles inputs where a > b by swapping them.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Ensure a is the lower bound and b is the upper bound\n    start = min(a, b)\n    end = max(a, b)\n\n    even_numbers = []\n    # Iterate from the lower bound to the upper bound (inclusive)\n    for num in range(start, end + 1):\n        # Check if the number is even\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_numbers.append(num)\n            \n    return even_numbers"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns even single-digit numbers between a and b (inclusive), in ascending order.\n    Numbers like 10, 12, 14 are excluded as they are not single digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n    \n    result = []\n    for num in range(min_val, max_val + 1):\n        if num % 2 == 0 and num >= 0 and num <= 9: # Check for even and single digit\n            result.append(num)\n            \n    return result\n```"}
